
Extension of the SM with  one complex DM particle which  has magnetic dipole moment and milli-charge

The
   make
commands compiles main.c and create executable ./main.

 ./main launched without arguments finds the dipole moment in [cm] units  which leads to Omegag^2=0.12 in
the freeze out scenario and the direct detection limit on the dipole moment for  DM masses in the interval  [1-1000]GeV

  ./main data*.par

reads parameters of the model presented in data*.par, calculates the relic density and determines the DD exclusion.
dataDM.par is an example where the dipole DM reproduces the relic density in the freeze in scenario and satisfies DD limit.
dataQ.par is an example of a  milli charge which  reproduces  the relic density in the freeze in scenario but is excluded by  DD limit.
